Negative control — the address description's COMPONENT ORDER (AC-31).

Mutates `mapAddress`'s `description` join: transposes `city` and `postcode`.

Should flip RED — __tests__/client-address.mappers.test.ts:
  - "AC-31 composes description as address_1, address_2, city, state,
     postcode, region, country"  (toBe oracleDescription)
  - "AC-31 keeps every component in the oracle's order — each one after the
     last"                       (indexOf positions must come out ascending)

Why THIS mutation, and not the previous one. The prior control dropped `state`
from the join. This API never returns `state` — it returns `county`, verified
live across all 98 recorded rows and by a `PUT {state}` that answered
`state: null` — so no recorded row can observe that mutation and it flipped
nothing. `city` and `postcode` are BOTH non-empty on
`recordedRowWithFullAddress()`, so transposing them is observable on real
recorded data.

